    "items": [
      {
        "text": "Jane Kim is an attorney who served on the San Francisco Board of Supervisors from 2011 to 2019. She served on the San Francisco Board of Education from 2006 to 2010. After leaving office she worked as California political director for Bernie Sanders' 2020 presidential campaign. She later served as state director for the California Working Families Party from January 2022 through January 2026.",
        "cites": [1, 2, 3, 4],
        "sentences": [
          {
            "text": "Jane Kim is an attorney who served on the San Francisco Board of Supervisors from 2011 to 2019.",
            "cites": [1]
          },
          {
            "text": "She served on the San Francisco Board of Education from 2006 to 2010.",
            "cites": [2]
          },
          {
            "text": "After leaving office she worked as California political director for Bernie Sanders' 2020 presidential campaign.",
            "cites": [3]
          },
          {
            "text": "She later served as state director for the California Working Families Party from January 2022 through January 2026.",
            "cites": [4]
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "text": "She proposes a state-run, nonprofit Natural Disaster Insurance for All program that would cover wildfire, flood and earthquake losses, funded by premiums. She wants to require home and auto insurers to pay out at least 65 to 75 cents in claims per premium dollar, similar to the federal minimum for health insurers. She proposes making insurers pay interest for each day they deny, delay or underpay a valid claim. Kim would audit the FAIR Plan governing committee and add seats for consumer advocates, the governor's office and the Department of Insurance. She proposes creating a Policyholder Bill of Rights with timely claim decisions, clear written explanations for denials and access to independent appraisal.",
        "cites": [5, 6, 7],
        "sentences": [
          {
            "text": "She proposes a state-run, nonprofit Natural Disaster Insurance for All program that would cover wildfire, flood and earthquake losses, funded by premiums.",
            "cites": [5]
