          {
            "text": "Kim would audit the FAIR Plan governing committee and add seats for consumer advocates, the governor's office and the Department of Insurance.",
            "cites": [6]
          },
          {
            "text": "She proposes creating a Policyholder Bill of Rights with timely claim decisions, clear written explanations for denials and access to independent appraisal.",
            "cites": [7]
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "text": "As supervisor, Kim helped secure free community college for city residents, the state's first $15 minimum wage ordinance and a tenant-protection ordinance against unjust evictions.",
